@page "/Account/NoAccess"

@* The #11 acceptance criteria's "you don't have access yet" page. Reachable two ways: directly from
   Dashboard.razor's inline role check, and as CookieAuthenticationOptions.AccessDeniedPath's target
   (configured in Program.cs) - nothing today declares an [Authorize(Roles=...)] policy that would redirect
   here on its own (the Role/UserRole schema exists per P2-3/#12, but no claim-minting yet - P2-5), but this
   page becomes that automatic target with no rework once one exists. See the P2-2 plan's Scope section for
   why this replaces the scaffold's separate AccessDenied page. *@

<PageTitle>No access yet</PageTitle>

<header>
    <h1>You don't have access yet</h1>
    <p>
        Your account is signed in, but it doesn't hold any role that grants access to the dashboard. If you
        believe this is a mistake, contact an Admin.
    </p>
</header>

<form action="Account/Logout" method="post">
    <AntiforgeryToken />
    <input type="hidden" name="ReturnUrl" value="" />
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary">Sign out</button>
</form>
